{
  "name": "Aga Khan University graduates media managers from boot camp",
  "parent_id": 203313841790202,
  "group_id": "4235eecf-0e09-443a-bafd-a99ed2852b91",
  "alternates": [],
  "created_at": "2026-07-31T09:38:00.753Z",
  "deleted_at": null,
  "sort_by_date": null,
  "tag_list": [],
  "updated_at": "2026-08-12T15:03:12.138Z",
  "published_at": "2026-08-12T15:03:12.125Z",
  "id": 203985226827821,
  "uuid": "27d33c95-88ef-44b9-8481-c141a3f22cd2",
  "is_folder": false,
  "content": {
    "_uid": "dbd90b78-74d1-2de9-18b7-db805d9d8b30",
    "body": [
      {
        "_uid": "0b6ca2d8-5914-afa9-c28f-abd5f0a621c5",
        "content": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "The seven-month training programme that is supported by the U.S. Embassy in Nairobi, brought together a diverse group of 20 editors and media managers from mainstream, community, and digital media platforms in Western Kenya. The programme exposed them to the fundamentals of media economics, international approaches to media challenges and new ways of thinking about digital solutions and innovation given the dynamic media environment.",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Speaking at the graduation, Professor Nancy Booker, Dean at GSMC reiterated the vital role the U.S. Embassy in Nairobi continues to play in assisting the School to train managers on how to navigate modern day journalism.",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": " \"Thanks to this programme, participants of the boot camp leave with essential tools to help them manage effectively. It has also grown their commitment to consistently seek to understand their teams, their audience, and the business aspects of journalism,\" she said.",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "As the media landscape continues to undergo unprecedented transformations driven by technological advancements and changing audience behaviors, the role of media managers has become increasingly pivotal.",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "In his remarks, the U.S. Embassy's Cultural Affairs Attaché Christopher Machin said \"The United States Embassy is pleased to collaborate with GSMC to facilitate this training programme. Kenya's media scene is witnessing the emergence of a new generation of innovators leveraging opportunities created by digital transformation. Offering a unique opportunity for U.S. and Kenyan experts to share their experiences and observations, this program equips participants with the skills to become future leaders in a rapidly evolving media industry.\"",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Professor George Nyabuga, Associate Professor at GSMC expressed his gratitude to the Embassy for the support and noted that the programme was in line with GSMC's mission to develop the capacity of journalists. \"Participants have learnt a lot and I hope that they will use the knowledge and skills to enhance the capacity of their media houses to report accurately, and provide the information and space Kenyans need to articulate issues that affect them and society.",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Throughout the programme, participants engaged in hands-on learning experiences, group projects, and immersive listening posts. The curriculum emphasized practical application, allowing participants to immediately implement their newfound knowledge and skills in their workplaces.",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
